/T (15 years have passed since the English Royal Court has disappeared into the great waves of the Atlantic Ocean. Yet, 15 years on the day, the Court reappeared from the ocean enlightened with the ways of Atlantis. However, the land that welcomed them back is now much changed and almost foreign from what they left. )
/E (15 years have passed since the English Royal Court has disappeared into the great waves of the Atlantic Ocean. Yet, 15 years on the day, the Court reappeared from the ocean enlightened with the ways of Atlantis. However, the land that welcomed them back is now much changed and almost foreign from what they left. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 87 0 R
/T (In your disappearance, France and Burgundy have entered into an alliance  and merged their territory. This new extra-large territory has also encroached upon England, invading England and taking over a fourth of the land. Thankfully, remaining English forces were able to stop efforts to restore Edward IV to the throne. A large party was thrown regardless by the Franco-Burgundians for their capture of the land, and during the merriment a new man slipped onto the throne. )
/E (In your disappearance, France and Burgundy have entered into an alliance  and merged their territory. This new extra-large territory has also encroached upon England, invading England and taking over a fourth of the land. Thankfully, remaining English forces were able to stop efforts to restore Edward IV to the throne. A large party was thrown regardless by the Franco-Burgundians for their capture of the land, and during the merriment a new man slipped onto the throne. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 87 0 R
/T (Instead of an Island ruled by Lancaster, York, or Tudor, they find a somewhat smelly man: Perkin Warbeck. This man claims to be one of the lost brothers from the Prince in the Tower incident. Having declared his claim in Burgundy's court, he won critical backing, and thus, for these last 15 years the British Isles have been under the control of this Burgundian-supported king. However, the nobles have not taken kindly to this rule, and they have been demanding for Parliament to gain back control. )
/E (Instead of an Island ruled by Lancaster, York, or Tudor, they find a somewhat smelly man: Perkin Warbeck. This man claims to be one of the lost brothers from the Prince in the Tower incident. Having declared his claim in Burgundy's court, he won critical backing, and thus, for these last 15 years the British Isles have been under the control of this Burgundian-supported king. However, the nobles have not taken kindly to this rule, and they have been demanding for Parliament to gain back control. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5 234 0 R 7 235 0 R 9]
