/T (As for the peasantry, not much has changed in the ways of their typical life. Many still face starvation, toil, and repression as Perkin Warbeck has elected to divert investments to his Burgundian supporters. This was made evermore evident when an outbreak of Sweats swept through the isles rampaging the populace. The hapless Perkin Warbeck was unable to fight back this pestilence as he found supporting a Burgundian war more important. )
