165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 88 0 R
/T (While Perkin Warbeck has been allowed to pursue Burgundian objectives, Parliament in the meantime has grown in influence. This Parliament is largely composed of Lancastrians who fell out of favor with the royal lines and sought power elsewhere. This sudden change in influence was only possible with the growing strength of the nobility as they filled in the void that Perkin Warbeck's rule had created. The growing noble class has used the momentum to tighten their control over their lands allowing many to disregard direct commands from King Warbeck. Nonetheless, the increased influence has not been felt within the king's court. Parliament has tried to exert influence through the power of the purse, however, the King has been able to ignore such brothers by dipping into the Burgundian treasury. )
/E (While Perkin Warbeck has been allowed to pursue Burgundian objectives, Parliament in the meantime has grown in influence. This Parliament is largely composed of Lancastrians who fell out of favor with the royal lines and sought power elsewhere. This sudden change in influence was only possible with the growing strength of the nobility as they filled in the void that Perkin Warbeck's rule had created. The growing noble class has used the momentum to tighten their control over their lands allowing many to disregard direct commands from King Warbeck. Nonetheless, the increased influence has not been felt within the king's court. Parliament has tried to exert influence through the power of the purse, however, the King has been able to ignore such brothers by dipping into the Burgundian treasury. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
